rota lap 5089, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the concrete fact at the door. context/TWO_ROOMS.md asks a page to name its room in **Status:** or **Room:**, and foundations/20260905-154954_the-clock-and-the-mark.md asks whether a number could turn out wrong. Both landed on this lap's own artifacts: the paper names mixed in both keys, and the tolerance figure is a census of work done rather than a forecast.
think The round opened on three files of mine standing in a round-open stash and on no ref, and the cold run named the guard that says so -- stash_record unlanded=2. Reds first, and two of the sixteen were mine.
think Read rather than redone, per petrichor's row. The parked paper was the ELDER scan shape, its figures one resolver-bound behind, and the landed 042700 reading supersedes it whole -- so it lands as testimony under a banner rather than as a second living reading.
think The landed reading raised one question and declined it: whether the static import graph, read as a lower bound, is enough to start a placement. That is the lane's work, so I took it.
think The first draft costed the computed layout against an unconstrained baseline and the layout LOST, 49 against 30.5. The reason is the finding: the true minimum of an unconstrained placement is every room on one node at cost zero, so the objective was asking for a capacity term.
think The capacity term turns out to be present where the traffic term is absent -- tracked non-symlink Rye bytes per room -- and it refuses the row's own unit before any weight arrives.
think Then the two drift models, which is what the lap is really for: scale drift keeps the edges and moves the numbers, structure drift moves the edges. Only one of them is ever named, and it is the harmless one.
obs A proxy's risk is structural rather than numeric. Scaling every weight by up to 256 leaves the layout exactly where it stood; moving two thirds of the edges is what takes it apart. That sentence reaches past row 7.
obs A placement reading without a size-matched baseline measures OCCUPANCY wearing a reading of coupling -- a node holding many rooms pays zero for the traffic inside it, so a piling layout wins under weights carrying no information at all. Size-matching costs the graph three points of credit.
obs The instrument proves itself from the far side: at total structural drift the computed layout finishes BEHIND chance by a tenth, which is what a layout built on an unrelated graph should do.
obs The awk LCG this tree writes elsewhere is a rounded shadow of the generator its comment names -- 20260912 * 1103515245 + 12345 is 22358225269615785 and awk computes 22358225269615784, above 2^53. Two tracked sites carry it; both spellings agree on this host, so it is named as a tell rather than booked as a red.
obs The card stands one byte under its ceiling after this account. A living pin at its ceiling taxes every lap a judgment call, and this one spent four rounds of trimming.
